<title>BELGIUM: EU says clears Schering/Gehe deal.</title>
<headline>EU says clears Schering/Gehe deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission confirmed on Wednesday it had cleared the acquisition by German drugs firm Schering AG of a 74.9-percent stake in Jenapharm GmbH, which was previously solely controlled by Gehe AG.</p>
<p>It noted that Schering and Jenapharm would see their share of the German markets for oral contraceptives and hormone therapy increase but competition from rival companies such as Akzo and Hoechst was strong.</p>
<p>Schering said earlier this week that the Commission had approved its venture with Gehe, the largest European pharmaceutical wholesaler.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
